

**15.3.12**: \(F(a,b;a+b-m;z)=\)\(\frac{\Gamma(m)\Gamma(a+b-m)}{\Gamma(a)\Gamma(b)}\)__\((1-z)^{-m}\sum\limits_{n=0}^{m-1}\frac{(a-m)_{n}(b-m)_{n}}{n!(1-m)_{n}}\)__\((1-z)^{n}\)__

\[\begin{array}{r@{\hspace{1em}}l}-\frac{(-1)^{m}\Gamma(a+b-m)}{\Gamma(a-m) \Gamma(b-m)}\sum\limits_{n=0}^{e}\frac{(a)_{n}(b)_{n}}{n!(n+m)!}\left(1-z\right) ^{n}\!\!\left[\ln\,\left(1-z\right)-\psi(n+1)\right.\\ \hskip 85.358268pt\left.-\psi(n+m+1)+\psi(a+n)+\psi(b+n)\right]\\ \hskip 85.358268pt\left(|\arg\,\left(1-z\right)|<\pi_{i}|1-z|<1\right)\end{array}\]

Similarly each term of 15.3.7 has a pole when \(b=a\pm m\) or \(b-a=\pm m\) and the case is covered by

**15.3.13**: \(F(a,a;c;z)=\)\(\frac{\Gamma(e)}{\Gamma(a)\Gamma(e-a)}\)__\((-z)^{-a}\sum\limits_{n=0}^{\infty}\frac{(a)_{n}(1-c+a)_{n}}{(n!)^{z}}\)__\(z^{-n}\!\!\left[\ln\,\left(-z\right)+2\psi(n+1)-\psi(a+n)-\psi(c-a-n)\right.\)__

The case \(b-a=m\), (\(m=1,2,3,\ .\ .\ .\) ) is covered by

**15.3.14**: \(F(a,a+m;c;z)=\)\(F(a+m,a;e;z)\)

\[\begin{array}{r@{\hspace{1em}}l}=\frac{\Gamma(c)(-z)^{-a-m}}{\Gamma(a+m)\Gamma (e-a)}\sum\limits_{n=0}^{e}\frac{(a)_{n+m}(1-c+a)_{n+m}}{n!(n+m)!}\,z^{-n}\!\! \left[\ln\,\left(-z\right)+\psi(1+m+n)+\psi(1+n)\right.\\ \hskip 85.358268pt\left.-\psi(a+m+n)-\psi(e-a-m-n)\right]+\left(-z\right)^{-a} \frac{\Gamma(c)}{\Gamma(a+m)}\sum\limits_{n=0}^{m-1}\frac{\Gamma(m-n)(a)_{n}}{ n!\Gamma(c-a-n)}\,z^{-n}\\ \hskip 85.358268pt\left(|\arg(-z)|<\pi_{i},|z|>1,(e-a)\neq 0,\pm 1,\pm 2,\ldots \right)\end{array}\]

The case \(e-a=0\), \(-1\), \(-2\), \(\therefore\) becomes elementary, 15.3.3, and the case \(c-a=1\), 2, 3, \(\therefore\) can be obtained from 15.3.14, by a limiting process (see [15.2]).



If, and only if the numbers \(\pm\,(1\!-\!e)\), \(\pm\,(a\!-\!b)\), \(\pm\,\langle a\!+\!b\!-\!c)\) are such, that two of them are equal or one of them is equal to \({{1\over 2}}\), then there exists a quadratic transformation. The basic formulae are due to Kummer [15.7] and a complete list is due to Goursat [15.3]. See also [15.2].

